From f211332ee8780986341569f700669dac58de765c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:40:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] target/microblaze: don't clobber reversed ld/st base

LOCAL ONLY: not for submission to qemu-devel (QEMU AI policy).
Reference for a hand-written fix.

do_load and do_store swizzle the address of a reversed sub-word
access in place:

	tcg_gen_xori_i32(addr, addr, 3 - size);

Since 36a9529e60 ("target/microblaze: Simplify
compute_ldst_addr_type{a,b}"), first released in v10.1.0,
compute_ldst_addr_typea returns cpu_R[ra] or cpu_R[rb] itself when the
other operand is r0, so lbur, lhur, sbr and shr now XOR the guest's
base register with 3 or 2.  With r5 = 0x90001000, "lbur r3, r5, r0"
leaves r5 = 0x90001003, and "shr r3, r0, r5" leaves 0x90001002.  When
both operands are r0 the address is a TCG constant, which must not be
written at all.

Swizzle into a new temporary instead, which is what the code did
before 36a9529e60, when compute_ldst_addr_typea always returned one.
lwr and swr are unaffected: a word access is not swizzled.

Fixes: 36a9529e60 ("target/microblaze: Simplify compute_ldst_addr_type{a,b}")
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/microblaze/translate.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/microblaze/translate.c b/target/microblaze/translate.c
index fefe5cb55..4eac13f36 100644
--- a/target/microblaze/translate.c
+++ b/target/microblaze/translate.c
@@ -718,7 +718,15 @@ static bool do_load(DisasContext *dc, int rd, TCGv_i32 addr, MemOp mop,
             mop ^= MO_BSWAP;
         }
         if (size < MO_32) {
-            tcg_gen_xori_i32(addr, addr, 3 - size);
+            /*
+             * ADDR may be a guest register or a constant, as returned
+             * by compute_ldst_addr_type{a,b}, so don't modify it in
+             * place.
+             */
+            TCGv_i32 t = tcg_temp_new_i32();
+
+            tcg_gen_xori_i32(t, addr, 3 - size);
+            addr = t;
         }
     }
 
@@ -878,7 +886,15 @@ static bool do_store(DisasContext *dc, int rd, TCGv_i32 addr, MemOp mop,
             mop ^= MO_BSWAP;
         }
         if (size < MO_32) {
-            tcg_gen_xori_i32(addr, addr, 3 - size);
+            /*
+             * ADDR may be a guest register or a constant, as returned
+             * by compute_ldst_addr_type{a,b}, so don't modify it in
+             * place.
+             */
+            TCGv_i32 t = tcg_temp_new_i32();
+
+            tcg_gen_xori_i32(t, addr, 3 - size);
+            addr = t;
         }
     }
 
